From fdeee827627f275d0a8e70ffd270f825e4e26a72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:48:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Add Tabs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A tab bar for moving between sibling panels of one record — Overview /
Activity / Files. Counts render as a pill that picks up the brand tint
when its tab is selected.

Ported from the Claude Design export and retokenised: the export carried
raw rgb() values and CSS-variable fallbacks, this version uses semantic
tokens only, so dark theme works without a second code path. No new
tokens were needed — the 10px count pill maps onto type.caption-sm and
the selected blue onto action.secondary.content.default.

Three changes from the export, all deliberate:

- The tabs now point at their panels. The export set role='tab' with no
  aria-controls and no ids, which announces a tab that controls nothing.
  Tabs now emits ids and aria-controls, and exports tabId()/tabPanelId()
  so the consumer can label the panel back. The WithPanels story is the
  full pattern.
- Keyboard support added. The export was mouse-only. The bar is now one
  tab stop with arrow keys moving within it, Home/End to the ends.
- Sizes are 32 / 40px (sm / md) rather than a single 36, matching Button
  and SegmentedControl, so md meets the 40px minimum target.

Also added countLabel, so a screen reader can hear '12 deliverables'
rather than 'Files 12'.
