From 33ea6794edde915fc001342ceae14556ed390cb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:56:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Tabs: fix the label colour and stop pointing at panels
 that aren't there
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two problems the a11y pass turned up once the stories were rendered in a
browser rather than only typechecked.

The unselected label was coming out black instead of text.tertiary. The
tab button was running its classes through cn(), and tailwind-merge files
any text-* utility it doesn't recognise under the colour group — so
text-label-lg and text-text-tertiary collided and the colour was dropped.
Moved 'group' into the class list so the button no longer needs cn() at
all. (The underlying tailwind-merge fault is fixed separately, in cn()
itself; this change makes Tabs correct either way.)

aria-controls now only appears when the caller passes idPrefix. Emitting
it unconditionally meant a bar rendered without panels pointed at ids
that don't exist — axe reports that as a critical violation, and it fired
on five of the seven stories. Opting in means a bare bar is incomplete
rather than wrong.

Also dropped an aria-selected:font-medium that never did anything:
type.label-lg already carries weight 500, so both states were 500. The
docs claimed a weight change; they no longer do.
